STANDARDS: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = [
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A01 Broken Access Control",
     "Enforce authorization server-side on every request. Deny by default. Check object ownership to prevent IDOR. Avoid path traversal when handling user supplied file paths."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A02 Cryptographic Failures",
     "Never hardcode secrets, API keys, passwords or private keys in source. Use strong hashing (argon2, bcrypt, PBKDF2) for passwords. Do not use MD5 or SHA1 for security. Enforce TLS and verify certificates."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A03 Injection",
     "Use parameterized queries and ORMs; never build SQL by string concatenation or f-strings. Avoid shell command construction from user input; avoid eval, exec and unsafe deserialization such as pickle or yaml.load. Escape output to prevent XSS; avoid innerHTML and dangerouslySetInnerHTML with untrusted data."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A04 Insecure Design",
     "Apply rate limiting, input validation and threat modeling. Separate trust boundaries and validate data crossing them."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A05 Security Misconfiguration",
     "Disable debug mode in production. Do not enable permissive CORS with credentials. Remove default credentials. Do not expose stack traces. Containers should not run as root."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A06 Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
     "Pin and regularly update dependencies. Remove unused packages. Monitor advisories for known CVEs."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A07 Identification and Authentication Failures",
     "Protect against credential stuffing and brute force. Use secure session handling and token expiry. Do not log credentials or tokens."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures",
     "Verify integrity of updates and dependencies. Avoid insecure deserialization. Secure CI/CD pipelines and do not curl-pipe-bash."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A09 Security Logging and Monitoring Failures",
     "Log authentication events and access control failures with enough context, without sensitive data."),
    ("OWASP Top 10", "A10 Server-Side Request Forgery",
     "Validate and allowlist outbound URLs derived from user input. Block requests to internal address ranges and metadata endpoints."),
    ("Style Guide", "Function size and complexity",
     "Keep functions short and focused, below roughly 50 lines. Deeply nested conditionals and very long files above 800 lines indicate a need to refactor into smaller modules."),
    ("Style Guide", "Layering and architecture",
     "Separate transport (routes), business logic (services) and persistence (repositories). Avoid circular dependencies and god classes. Keep configuration in one place driven by environment variables."),
    ("Style Guide", "Error handling",
     "Do not swallow exceptions with bare except or empty catch blocks. Handle errors explicitly and log them with context."),
    ("Style Guide", "Testing and documentation",
     "Provide automated tests for core logic and a README describing setup and architecture. Avoid leaving TODO and FIXME markers unresolved in production code."),
]
